AI assistance was used for this change. I reviewed and tested it.

oxfmt deletes a decorator on a rest parameter. This happens with the default settings, and oxfmt reports no error.

```ts
class C {
  m(@Dec() ...args: string[]) {}
}

// before
class C {
  m(...args: string[]) {}
}
```

The parser and codegen support these decorators (#18938, #20132), but the formatter printed only the rest element and its type annotation. This PR prints the decorators in the same way as for `FormalParameter`.

The new fixture `ts/parameters/rest-decorators.ts` covers single and multiple decorators, `@(await p)`, a decorator after another parameter, and long parameter lists. The output matches Prettier 3.9.10 for every case.

